# Normalize line endings for a multi-platform repo.
#
# Every text file is stored with LF in the repository and checked out with
# LF everywhere.  This matters beyond style: tests/test_lifecycle.py embeds
# POSIX shell fixtures (#!/bin/sh scripts written to disk and exec'd), which
# silently break as "bad interpreter" when a Windows checkout rewrites them
# with CRLF.  All tooling here (python, node, java, browsers) reads LF fine,
# so forcing LF costs nothing and removes the whole CRLF-corruption class.
* text=auto eol=lf

# True binary assets — never normalize.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
